# Vibe Coding Cost Efficient

## Objective

Keep AI-assisted development fast and cheap by avoiding redundant reads, re-analysis, and unnecessary tool calls, without sacrificing correctness.

## Core Principles

- Reuse context already gathered earlier in the session (see context-caching, project-memory) instead of rereading files.
- Read only files actually relevant to the current task.
- Avoid duplicate analysis of the same code/structure.
- Prefer incremental, targeted changes over broad exploratory rewrites.

## Requirements

- Check whether needed information was already established earlier in the session before re-fetching it.
- Scope file reads to the relevant section/function when the file is large.
- Batch related tool calls instead of many small sequential ones where the tool supports it.
- Cache architectural knowledge (stack, structure, conventions) gathered during the session and reuse it.

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- Re-reading the same file repeatedly for information already captured.
- Reading entire large files when only a specific function/section is relevant.
- Re-deriving already-established project facts from scratch each turn.

## Self Review

Before considering work complete, verify:

✓ No redundant file reads or re-analysis occurred for already-known information.
✓ Tool usage was proportional to the actual task, not exploratory beyond need.
✓ Correctness was preserved — efficiency never came at the cost of a wrong or incomplete answer.

## Golden Rule

Minimize tool usage and token spend, but never at the expense of correctness.
